  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be a function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math> is equal to :"
  },
